00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:03.580
In this video, I'm going to demonstrate
how you can use the slide master view

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:08.170
to make changes to one slide which will
then be applied to every subsequent slide

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:10.080
that you insert into the presentation.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:16.830
So what I need to do is I need to navigate
up to the view tab and under view tab,

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:18.660
I would need to select slide master.

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:23.160
So I select slide master, that will
take me into slide master view.

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:26.730
Look, don't worry too much that
all of the information from your

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:29.100
original presentation isn't visible.

00:00:29.189 --> 00:00:30.390
It is actually still there.

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:35.340
All this is doing is it's defining
the content, the layout, the design,

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:39.930
the fonts, the background images and
the theme that you may be using or

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:42.570
wish to use for each presentation.

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:47.400
So one of the things to remember is
that if you wish to make a change

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:50.910
that will be applied to all slides,
you need to select slide one.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:53.880
Now I'm going to insert the company logo.

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:55.680
And so I've selected slide one.

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:59.699
And all I need to do then is go
to the insert tab, select picture

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:05.340
from this device, navigate to the
image, double click on the image

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:07.590
and it inserts it into the slide.

00:01:08.475 --> 00:01:12.615
I can just move that up to the top and
then I'll resize that, make it quite small

00:01:13.545 --> 00:01:19.545
and also change the transparency so it
isn't very clear and I'm happy with that.

00:01:20.055 --> 00:01:24.795
Again, if I make a change to the font,
so if I changed the font there, if I

00:01:24.795 --> 00:01:28.845
go to the home tab and it's Calibri
Light, headings 44 at the moment, if

00:01:28.845 --> 00:01:34.515
I change that to Arial and, say, 54.

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:38.170
When I come out of the slide master.

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:41.440
So I have to click on the slide
master tab again, and close slide

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:46.080
master view that will automatically
change the size of the font.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:52.020
And as you can also see, the image
has been placed at the top of every

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:53.580
slide within the presentation.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:58.650
If I go to a new slide and
select a blank slide again.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:04.770
And, and then add another title slide it
automatically adds that and the font is

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:08.220
automatically going to be Arial size 60.

00:02:09.359 --> 00:02:15.120
So if I go back to the view and select
slide master again, go back to slide one.

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:17.130
I can also change the theme.

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:20.040
So if I decided that I wasn't
happy with the theme that I had

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:23.910
